  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin no later than three years from the date of this decision.  \r\nReason:  To accord with the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 3, Paragraph MA.2 (5) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).  \r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved drawings:  109_A-080_PD, 109_A-090_PD, 109_A-095_PD (Rev 01), 109-A-100_PD, 109_A-101_PD, 109_A-102_PD, 109_A-103_PD, 109_A-110_PD (Rev 01), 109_A-111_PD (Rev 01), 109_A-112_PD (Rev 01), 109_A-200_PD  Received:  05 February 2025.  \r\nReason:  In accord with the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 3, Paragraph W.12 (a) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).  \r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - Prior to the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, the Local Planning Authority shall be informed of the agreed naming and numbering of the proposed dwellings so that arrangements can be put in place to ensure that, with the exception of a person eligible for a disabled person's badge issued pursuant to Section 21 of the Chronically Sick and Disabled Persons Act 1970 (or similar legislation), no resident of the development shall obtain a resident's parking permit.  Any occupiers of the approved development shall surrender any such permit wrongly issued or held.  \r\nReason:  To accord with the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 3, Paragraph MA.2 (2(a)) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).  \r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, the twenty eight resident cycle parking spaces located in the building's rear amenity area included in the submitted Proposed Ground Floor Plan (Ref:  109_A-110_PD Rev 01) shall be implemented with fourteen Sheffield stands each spaced by one metre between each stand and from the adjoining boundary treatments, made available for use before the development is occupied and permanently retained for use at all times without obstruction thereafter.  \r\nReason: In order to support sustainable transport objectives in accordance with Schedule 2, Part 3, Paragraph MA.2 (2(a)) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The site's existing secure fenced waste storage compound, as shown in the submitted Proposed Ground Floor Plan (Ref:  109_A-110_PD Rev 01), shall be retained for the storage of the communal residual waste, recyclable material and food waste wheelie bins for the fifteen flats hereby permitted, in accordance with the Recycling and Refuse Guidance:  Guide for Architects and Planners (2022).  All communal residual waste, recyclable material and food waste wheelie bins for the fifteen flats hereby permitted shall be stored within this compound at all times when not being emptied.  \r\n\r\nNo alteration to the existing waste storage compound's fences, gates or area shall be made without the submission of details for the approval of the Local Planning Authority, and be implemented and permanently retained in accordance with any such approved details.  \r\n\r\nPrior to the occupation of any flat hereby permitted and notwithstanding the submitted Proposed Ground Floor Plan (Ref:  109_A-110_PD Rev 01) and Proposed Site Plan (Ref:  109_A-095_PD Rev:  01), details for the collection of communal waste and recycling bins, including for the entry and egress of waste collection vehicles to and from the site and its private access road, and any waste collection point and associated hard standing provided within the private access road's southern side grass verge shall be submitted for the approval of the Local Planning Authority, and be implemented and permanently adhered to thereafter.  \r\n\r\nReason:  In order to ensure adequate storage provision and collection arrangements (in the context of the site's access constraints) for waste and recycled materials in accordance with Schedule 2, Part 3, Paragraph MA.2 (2(a)) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).  \r\n"
  ],
